    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1466">

                <pb facs="0955" n="839" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg839"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/30.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your note of August 31, wherein you suggest that, when American
                    Consular officers or other officials in Mexico receive intimation of any steps
                    or events likely to affect the safety of foreigners, they may at once impart
                    their knowledge to all foreigners alike.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to advise you that instructions in the sense indicated had already
                    been given to all American Consuls in Mexico.</p>
                <p>In this relation I beg also to advise you that the United States Transport <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Buford</hi>, now on the west coast of Mexico for the
                    purpose of bringing out refugees, has been instructed to furnish transportation
                    to any foreigners who desire to leave Mexico, in so far as the capacity of the
                    vessel will permit.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
